    {
      "heading": "Spotting sarcasm",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Read this. Brilliant planning. The only tap is behind a locked door.",
          "write": "\"Brilliant planning…\""
        },
        {
          "say": "Circle the loaded word. Brilliant sounds positive.",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 300,
            "alt": "Positive word, bad situation",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 30,
                "y": 60,
                "w": 220,
                "h": 80,
                "fill": "green",
                "change": "highlight",
                "label": "“Brilliant”"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 310,
                "y": 60,
                "w": 220,
                "h": 80,
                "fill": "red",
                "label": "locked tap"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 140,
                "y": 180,
                "text": "nice words",
                "size": 20,
                "color": "black",
                "anchor": "middle"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 420,
                "y": 180,
                "text": "nasty situation",
                "size": 20,
                "color": "black",
                "anchor": "middle"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "But the situation is bad. The words and situation don't match.",
          "write": "words ≠ situation"
        },
        {
          "say": "Nice words plus a nasty situation means sarcasm.",
          "write": "= sarcastic",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 300,
            "alt": "Sarcasm",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 30,
                "y": 60,
                "w": 220,
                "h": 80,
                "fill": "green",
                "label": "“Brilliant”"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 310,
                "y": 60,
                "w": 220,
                "h": 80,
                "fill": "red",
                "label": "locked tap"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 280,
                "y": 220,
                "text": "= SARCASTIC",
                "size": 32,
                "color": "purple",
                "anchor": "middle",
                "bold": true,
                "change": "add"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "Admiring is the trap. Brilliant isn't meant sincerely here.",
          "write": "✗ admiring"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Connotation",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Words with similar meanings can carry different feelings.",
          "write": "connotation = feeling"
        },
        {
          "say": "Cosy and cramped can both describe a small room.",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 300,
            "alt": "Cosy versus cramped",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 40,
                "y": 60,
                "w": 200,
                "h": 140,
                "fill": "orange",
                "label": "cosy"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 320,
                "y": 60,
                "w": 200,
                "h": 140,
                "fill": "grey",
                "label": "cramped"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 140,
                "y": 240,
                "text": "feels warm",
                "size": 20,
                "color": "green",
                "anchor": "middle",
                "change": "add"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 420,
                "y": 240,
                "text": "feels uncomfortable",
                "size": 20,
                "color": "red",
                "anchor": "middle",
                "change": "add"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "Cosy feels warm. Cramped feels uncomfortable.",
          "write": "cosy (+)   cramped (−)"
        },
        {
          "say": "Writers pick the word whose feeling suits their purpose."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Persuasive techniques",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Emotive language makes readers feel strongly.",
          "write": "rip the heart out of our town"
        },
        {
          "say": "A rhetorical question makes the answer seem obvious.",
          "write": "Don't we all deserve to feel safe?"
        },
        {
          "say": "Inclusive words like we and our put readers on your side.",
          "write": "we • our • let's"
        },
        {
          "say": "Statistics and experts make it seem reliable. An anecdote makes it personal.",
          "write": "evidence • anecdote"
        },
        {
          "say": "Repetition and the rule of three make it memorable.",
          "write": "Every day… every day… every day"
        },
        {
          "say": "Always name the technique, then its effect on the reader.",
          "write": "uses ___ to make the reader ___",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 300,
            "alt": "Technique leads to effect",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 30,
                "y": 90,
                "w": 200,
                "h": 80,
                "fill": "blue",
                "label": "Technique"
              },
              {
                "kind": "arrow",
                "x": 240,
                "y": 130,
                "x2": 320,
                "y2": 130,
                "color": "purple",
                "change": "add"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 330,
                "y": 90,
                "w": 200,
                "h": 80,
                "fill": "green",
                "change": "add",
                "label": "Effect"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Figurative language",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "A simile compares using like or as.",
          "write": "snores like distant thunder"
        },
        {
          "say": "A metaphor says one thing is another.",
          "write": "the library was the jewel",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 300,
            "alt": "Simile has like or as, metaphor does not",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 30,
                "y": 60,
                "w": 230,
                "h": 90,
                "fill": "teal",
                "label": "Simile: like / as"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 300,
                "y": 60,
                "w": 230,
                "h": 90,
                "fill": "orange",
                "label": "Metaphor: is"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 145,
                "y": 200,
                "text": "snores like thunder",
                "size": 18,
                "color": "black",
                "anchor": "middle"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 415,
                "y": 200,
                "text": "was the jewel",
                "size": 18,
                "color": "black",
                "anchor": "middle"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 280,
                "y": 260,
                "text": "Like or as? Simile it has.",
                "size": 22,
                "color": "purple",
                "anchor": "middle",
                "bold": true,
                "change": "highlight"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "Personification gives human qualities to things. The wind begged to come in.",
          "write": "the wind begged"
        },
        {
          "say": "Hyperbole exaggerates. It took a million years!",
          "write": "hyperbole = exaggeration"
        },
        {
          "say": "Irony says the opposite of what's meant, or the opposite happens.",
          "write": "irony"
        }
      ]
    },
